# Steam Deck GAMING-ONLY packages (FAST-INSTALL.md C2).
#
# Installed offline from the bundled mirror for Gaming=yes installs only --
# by the early optional delta (which reads this file from
# /usr/share/omarchy-iso/deck-gaming.packages on the LIVE ISO), and later by
# /usr/bin/omarchy-deck-enable-gaming for the C6 desktop opt-in. Gaming=no
# installs none of this; the common minimal root image excludes all of it.
#
# ⚠️ BARE NAMES, never repo-qualified. This list is resolved against the
# single-repo OFFLINE mirror (configs/pacman-offline.conf declares exactly
# one repo); a `jupiter-staging/foo` entry aborts that resolve the same way
# it would in deck-install.packages. The offline mirror carries exactly one
# build of gamescope -- Valve's, because builder/build-iso.sh downloads the
# qualified `jupiter-staging/gamescope` (see deck-mirror.packages) and strips
# the bare form from the download list -- so bare `gamescope` here resolves
# to Valve's build, the ONLY one shipping
# usr/share/wayland-sessions/gamescope-wayland.desktop.
#
# ONLINE consumers must re-qualify: against the online repos a bare
# `gamescope` resolves by repo order to Arch's extra build, which ships no
# session file. omarchy-deck-enable-gaming therefore installs
# `jupiter-staging/gamescope` (qualified) plus the bare names below. The
# mapping is stated here so the two consumers cannot drift: bare name <->
# online name is identity for every entry except gamescope.
#
# --- Gaming Mode's session file (deck-install.packages §14.6, moved here) ----
#
# READER: the early gaming delta + the C6 opt-in, offline from the mirror.
#
# Valve's build ships /usr/share/wayland-sessions/gamescope-wayland.desktop,
# the file deck_autologin.py's GAMING_SESSION looks for. Without it an
# install completes and lands in DESKTOP mode. DUAL ENTRY with
# `jupiter-staging/gamescope` in deck-mirror.packages (which decides the
# build); this file decides THAT it is installed.
gamescope

# --- The two vulkan-driver pins (deck-install.packages §3.8, moved here) -----
#
# READER: the early gaming delta + the C6 opt-in, offline from the mirror.
#
# `steam` depends on the VIRTUAL packages `vulkan-driver` and
# `lib32-vulkan-driver`. With no AMD provider selected, pacman picks the
# NVIDIA stack on its own and nothing errors. Naming both pins makes the
# outcome independent of resolver order. They must land BEFORE the online
# `steam` fetch (deck-fetch.packages): the fetch resolves steam's virtual
# deps against a target that already provides them. Moved here (not deleted)
# because Gaming=no never fetches steam, so unconditional pins would drag
# the NVIDIA question -- and the driver weight -- into a desktop-only image.
vulkan-radeon
lib32-vulkan-radeon

# --- Gaming Mode's performance overlay (moved here) ---------------------------
#
# READER: the early gaming delta + the C6 opt-in, offline from the mirror.
#
# `mangohud`/`lib32-mangohud` ship /usr/bin/mangoapp, which Valve's
# gamescope-mangoapp.service and src/deck-session.sh both expect. Arch's
# 0.8.4-1 is NEWER than Valve's 0.8.3-4 and already carries mangoapp, so
# these stay BARE and resolve to Arch's build -- do not qualify them into
# jupiter-staging/ to match gamescope. DUAL ENTRY with deck-mirror.packages,
# which keeps its copy so the "which build" decision stays where the
# measurement is written down.
mangohud
lib32-mangohud
